  "gloss": "because",
  "title": "karena — because",
  "pattern": "A karena B · Karena B, A",
  "explanation": "karena gives the reason. It usually comes after the main point: Saya pulang karena capek. — I'm going home because I'm tired. The reason can also come first, followed by a comma: Karena hujan, kami di rumah saja. When both halves have the same subject you can leave it out after karena (karena capek, not always karena saya capek), and karena works before a single word where English needs because of: karena macet, because of the traffic.",
  "natural": "The neutral because, right in polite and careful speech and in writing: with staff, a doctor, a teacher or someone older, and when someone asks you Kenapa? (why?).",
  "stiff": "Not stiff, but among friends soalnya (next lesson) is the chattier choice. sebab means the same and sounds more formal.",
